 "notes": [
  "On 1h, BBW below 0.02 gave 34,735 entries in 1,268 separate moves. Twenty candles later they were 0.13% behind random entries, inside the luck band. BBW below its 10th percentile of the last 150 bars did 0.18% worse than random, just below the band. That holds without its strongest stretch (May 26–28, 2021) and at 10 candles, but not at 50 or 100. SOL alone was 0.4% behind random, and BTC and ETH were inside their bands.",
  "After BBW crossed up through 0.10 on 1h, price was 0.55% ahead of random entries after 20 candles, against a band that tops out at 0.31%. It holds without its strongest stretch and at 10, 20, 50 and 100 candles. These crosses come in volatile candles, and the random copies keep their timing but not the volatility. In a window where price rose, a long that enters as volatility jumps will tend to show bigger gains, so read it as price moving more after the cross, not as a call on direction.",
  "The per-coin split of that 1h cross is thin. SOL was 0.63% ahead and holds at every horizon. BTC at 0.34% and ETH at 0.36% each vanish once a single stretch is left out, on Jan 13, 2021 for BTC and Jan 2–3, 2021 for ETH. On 4h the same cross is inside the luck band pooled, and on SOL it did 1.18% worse than random.",
  "BBW above its 90th percentile on 1h beat random by 0.17%, barely over the band edge of 0.16%. The result comes from 38 entries on Nov 6–7, 2020, and without them it is chance. It is also chance at 10, 50 and 100 candles. These are volatile candles too, so any gain reflects when they fire, in a window that rose. On 4h and daily it is inside the band.",
  "BBW crossing down through 0.05 on 1h did 0.18% worse than random. That holds without its strongest stretch and at 10 and 100 candles, but not at 50. On 4h it is inside the band, and on daily it fired too rarely to judge, with 10 entries. On daily, BBW below its 10th percentile gave only 73 moves and landed inside the band.",
  "For a long DCA bot on 1h, a squeeze start condition gave entries no better than random, and the 10th-percentile version slightly worse. The take profit and DCA orders still do the work there. BBW crossing up through 0.10 is better used as a volatility condition beside a directional filter, with the take profit and DCA step sized for bigger moves. In a falling market the same burst of volatility moves price down just as hard, so it is no reason to go long on its own."
